## 1. Definitions

For purposes of this License:

**"SmaulBRAIN"** means the software, source code, documentation, configuration, model implementation, training implementation, tools, scripts, and other materials distributed under this License.

**"Original Work"** means the version of SmaulBRAIN originally published by the copyright holder and any contributions accepted into the project.

**"Covered Work"** means the Original Work and any work that copies, incorporates, modifies, translates, ports, or is otherwise substantially derived from the source code of SmaulBRAIN.

**"Derivative Work"** means a work that contains, incorporates, modifies, or is substantially based on protected source code from SmaulBRAIN.

**"Service"** means software or infrastructure made available to users over a network, including but not limited to an API, website, hosted application, cloud service, inference service, model-serving service, or SaaS product.

**"Commercial Use"** means using a Covered Work, directly or indirectly, to obtain payment, revenue, profit, monetary compensation, paid access, or other commercial consideration from users or customers.

Commercial Use includes, but is not limited to:

* selling API requests or tokens;
* selling inference credits;
* charging subscriptions for access;
* charging users for hosted access;
* selling access to a SmaulBRAIN-based model or service;
* selling a SmaulBRAIN-based application;
* licensing a Covered Work as proprietary software;
* placing a Covered Work behind a paid service;
* charging customers for access to functionality substantially provided by a Covered Work;
* incorporating a Covered Work into a paid product or service.

**"Permission"** means explicit authorization granted by the copyright holder of SmaulBRAIN. Permission must be granted in writing through an official project communication channel, including a GitHub issue, GitHub discussion, or email.

